**Step 3. Texts by program (dry run):** build the comment (fill-ins applied by program; the payload equals the kit's text with only the fill-ins changed: program check, by sha256 against the kit line and the frozen hash), the new ticket's summary and six paragraphs (same check against both frozen hashes), the entry and the three appended texts; print them; run the scan (0 problems, controls fire); check each file:line fragment named in a text against its source and each relayed fact against its status-file line; no `<<` left; the table (key, class, length, sha256, marker, check printed yes/no). Run the WHOLE write path against a FAKE transport (canned 2xx) and print the request list (1 comment, the move slot MOVE allows, the create slot CREATE allows, nothing else); the fence tests of Step 1 refused there too. JIRA slot HOLD stops here (`RECORDS DRY RUN ONLY`).
